{
  "$comment": [
    "The user-facing documentation contract. Read by scripts/audit-doc-freshness.ps1.",
    "",
    "Each entry binds ONE user-facing document to the source paths it describes.",
    "That binding is what makes Google's 'Update Docs with Code' rule mechanical",
    "instead of aspirational: if a coupled source changes in a push and the doc",
    "does not, the gate fails.",
    "",
    "'sources' are path PREFIXES matched against the changed-file list.",
    "'maxAgeDays' bounds how stale the '**Last verified:**' stamp may get.",
    "Add a doc here the moment it becomes user-facing. Docs NOT listed here are",
    "internal design/phase notes and are deliberately not gated."
  ],
